course: dictionary
lesson: 10519
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and type is one of them. The words around it tell you which meaning is right. «A type of fruit» means a kind or sort of fruit, so the word is about sorting things into groups.
explain: «Ruby in Perth watched her big brother type his phone code» is different. Here type is a doing word, and it means pressing keys to write or enter something. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check: "watched her brother press keys to enter his phone code" still makes sense.
explain: Ask yourself whether the word is a thing or an action. «There are four types» means there are four kinds, so type is a naming word here. When a word could mean two things, read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Type» as a naming word means a kind or sort of something, like «a type of fruit».
fact: «Type» as a doing word means to press keys to write on a computer, phone or typewriter.
fact: A blood type is the group your blood belongs to.
fact: «Not my type» means not the kind of person or thing I like.
exercise: «A type of fruit» is in a list of fruit. What does type mean here? | Not the kind of person I like | *A kind or sort of something | To press keys to write | A blood group
exercise: «Ruby watched her brother type his phone code.» What does type mean here? | A sort of game | *To press keys to write or enter something | A kind of phone | To drop something on the floor
exercise: «There are four types.» How many types are there? | Two | Ten | Three | *Four
test: What is a blood type? | A sort of sweet | A kind of computer | *The group your blood belongs to | A game you play at school
test: «Not my type» means what? | *Not the kind of person or thing I like | The sort of sport I play | Something I type very fast | A kind of computer
exam: In «a type of phone», what does type mean? | Not my type | *A kind or sort | A blood group | To press keys
